 efficiency +10% and the order limit +4"},{"name":"Inspiration","facility":"Dormitory","eliteLevel":"Base","description":"When this Operator is assigned to a Dormitory, restores +0.1 Morale per hour to all Operators assigned to that Dormitory (Only the strongest effect of this type takes place)"}],"modules":[{"type":"Original","name":"April's Badge","stages":[]},{"type":"Upgrade","name":"MAR-Y: Hi-Fi Headset","mission":{"requirement1":"During battle, deploy April a total of 8 times (excluding Support Units)","requirement2":"Clear Main Theme 5-3 with a 3-star rating; You must deploy your own April, and have April defeat at least 2 Spec Ops Caster Leaders"},"stages":[{"stage":"Stage 1","attributesIncreased":"HP +110 , ATK +23","effectLabel":"New trait","effectText":"When there are ground enemies within range, ASPD +8","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":2},{"name":"Manganese Trihydrate","quantity":3},{"name":"LMD","quantity":40000}]},{"stage":"Stage 2","attributesIncreased":"HP +160 , ATK +28","effectLabel":"Experienced Hunter improved","effectText":"Redeployment Time -25 seconds, DP Cost -2","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":2},{"name":"Data Supplement Stick","quantity":20},{"name":"Polymerized Gel","quantity":4},{"name":"LMD","quantity":50000}]},{"stage":"Stage 3","attributesIncreased":"HP +190 , ATK +32","effectLabel":"Experienced Hunter improved","effectText":"Redeployment Time -28 seconds, DP Cost -2","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":2},{"name":"Data Supplement Instrument","quantity":8},{"name":"Optimized Device","quantity":5},{"name":"LMD","quantity":60000}]}]}],"review":{"official":"A hunter from\nRim Billiton\n, lost her job due to\nOripathy\nbefore making her way to\nRhodes Island\n.\nHas never received formal training. All indicators read average. Her previous occupation suggested an affinity for sniper training, and she currently serves as a\nSniper\nOperator\n.","editor":null,"rating":null},"synergies":[],"techniques":[{"technique":null,"techniqueDescription":null,"description":null}],"guides":[],"stats":{"phases":[{"elite":0,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":50,"base":{"hp":572,"atk":178,"def":56,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":11,"block":1,"interval":1},"max":{"hp":818,"atk":298,"def":94,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":11,"block":1,"interval":1},"rangeId":"3-1"},{"elite":1,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":70,"base":{"hp":818,"atk":298,"def":94,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":13,"block":1,"interval":1},"max":{"hp":1049,"atk":432,"def":135,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":13,"block":1,"interval":1},"rangeId":"3-3"},{"elite":2,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":80,"base":{"hp":1049,"atk":432,"def":135,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":13,"block":1,"interval":1},"max":{"hp":1280,"atk":528,"def":160,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":13,"block":1,"interval":1},"rangeId":"3-3"}],"trust":{"hp":0,"atk":75,"def":0}},"files":[{"section":"Clinical Analysis","unlock":"Unlocked at 25 trust","description":"Imaging tests have shown the outlines of her internal organs to be indistinct due to abnormal shadows. Originium granules have been detected in her circulatory system, confirming her to be infected with Oripathy.\n\n [Cell-Originium Assimilation] 5%\nSome mild crystallization visible on her back. \n\n[Blood Originium-Crystal Density] 0.17u/L\nThe Operator reports she avoided dangerous environments with significant Originium exposure risk, but living in such poor conditions for so long ultimately caused her infection to worsen."},{"section":"Archive File 1","unlock":"Unlocked at 50 trust","description":"She has a real urban feel to her, always going around with her stereo playing.\nVery extroverted, she gets along with everyone. \nShe is always looking to improve her lot in life, and follows trends closely. She is often seen chatting with Utage and Orchid."},{"section":"Archive File 2","unlock":"Unlocked at 100 trust","description":"Because of the highly developed mining industry in Rim Billiton, the population is more likely to be exposed to Originium than in other countries. So most Rim Billiton companies have some kind of benefits structure for employees who get infected on the job to encourage them to work without fear. \nBut April's experience shows that not every company does provide such benefits. Or maybe because of a general revulsion for Infected people, the lower level functionaries of these companies may not have an interest in caring for them, no matter what policies the upper management may put in place to keep people working.\nWhether April was forced out of Rim Billiton because her benefits weren't worth the paper they were printed on, or because a bad actor worked against her, we can't know. And it's clear she hasn't investigated it herself. Of course, it doesn't really matter, in the end. Even if it is the latter, it wouldn't be easy for April to go recover what is owed her, considering the situation of the Infected."},{"section":"Archive File 3","unlock":"Unlocked at 150 trust","description":"If Rhodes Island held an interior decorating competition (we won't), then April would likely take the prize. \nRhodes Island dormitories have a very plain design, serving only to provide occupants with a basic standard of living. Most operators have no further interest in design. But the company does not have any regulations against operators making interior modifications, as long as they don't damage the landship. In fact, Rhodes Island encourages them to do just that, in hopes of improving their lives. So while most operators live in very plain surroundings, there are some with a lot of character, and April's are among the best. \nHer room is exquisitely decorated. Posters, knick knacks, flower pots, and such all give the place a lively atmosphere, well-suited to her personality. We're very glad to see her adapting to and even loving life at Rhodes Island."},{"section":"Archive File 4","unlock":"Unlocked at 200 trust","description":"There is a common misconception that once someone becomes Infected, they will then speak for the Infected, and always side with the Infected. \nThe truth is obviously different. Sudden changes are always difficult to accept. One who does try to accept such changes should be commended for her open-mindedness. But we shouldn't condemn someone for failing to accept the drastic, sudden change that is Oripathy infection.\nNot everyone would openly accept her identity as an Infected person, and every new Rhodes Island operator will receive psychological counseling about that identity to avoid excessive burdens and conflicts over the course of her work. \nThis is of particular concern for operators who come from civilian backgrounds like April, for whom discrimination against the Infected is deeply rooted. We must acknowledge the reality that some people, completely without malice, grow up in an environment that teaches them to dehumanize the Infected. And that these people, even if they become Infected themselves, do not see the Infected as peers. It is difficult to reverse that perception. \nLuckily, April's cheerful disposition and open-minded personality did her well. While she had some ingrained discrimination against the Infected and some resultant self-loathing, she quickly shed these ideas thanks to our counseling and the general environment of life in Rhodes Island. She immediately began to think about how she could help others who also suffered like her. While she may not be that impressive in combat, April's outlook and thinking are worthy of emulation."}]},"appearances":[{"label":"Base","iconPath":"/five-star-icons/April%20-%20Base.webp","fullPath":"/five-star-skins/April%20-%20Base.webp"},{"label":"Elite 2","iconPath":"/five-star-icons/April%20-%20Elite%202.webp","fullPath":"/five-star-skins/April%20-%20Elite%202.webp"},{"label":"Faraway Gaze","iconPath":"/five-star-icons/April%20-%20Faraway%20Gaze.webp","fullPath":"/five-star-skins/April%20-%20Faraway%20Gaze.webp"}],"skinObtainByLabel":{"Faraway Gaze":"15 OP"},"synergyMatches":[],"a